Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:18:17 +0800
Subject: Adapt the pinned build tools to the supported runner environments

Upstream-Status: Local build compatibility
Maintenance: Drop each workaround when the pinned upstream handles its compiler, host architecture or Visual Studio version.
Tests: Native consumer matrix; Linux ARM64 system Clang and Windows toolchain discovery.
Original-Recipe: c755c8163a2702c822eaf875ce52c1d02823e267 patches/host-tools.patch

Base: rusty_v8 v0.106.0 (e9f20a2493883b53cb58b19a2fe761358dd57996),
including its Chromium build submodule at
c6d44e625aa64fa89cbdc971dfd301353bee04f3.

These are build-host compatibility adjustments, not V8 feature cuts:

- Map Linux's aarch64 machine name to arm64 for the pinned GN/Ninja package
  names. The existing Windows mapping selects the available x64 tools;
  Windows ARM64 can execute them through Windows emulation. That mapping
  remains from the earlier ARM64 experiment and does not imply support:
  Windows ARM64 is excluded from the current build and release matrix.
- Restrict the ARM64 branch's Linux sysroot downloads to Linux targets.
  macOS and Windows do not need those Linux sysroots. Linux retains the
  upstream sysroot selection; this patch does not change its glibc baseline.
- When using a system Clang on Linux, ask that compiler for its target's
  compiler-rt builtins archive. Distribution packages do not necessarily
  match Chromium's directory layout. Pass the existing file through a
  dedicated GN argument affecting only compiler_builtins, leaving other
  clang_lib targets on their original path. Linux ARM64 CI supplies Clang
  18 and its matching compiler-rt development package; this is separate
  from the Linux sysroot and does not replace it.
- Recognize Visual Studio 2026, its installation directory named 18, and
  its VC145 runtime directory. The pinned discovery code knows only older
  versions. Keep the existing version-selection and override mechanism;
  this change adds a discovery option, not a requirement to use VS 2026.

Validation: build and run the standalone archive consumer on the affected
supported platforms. Linux ARM64 exercises the system-Clang path, macOS
ARM64 exercises the sysroot guard, and Windows x64 exercises the selected
Visual Studio installation. A Windows run using VS 2022 does not validate
VS 2026 discovery. The separate glibc 2.23 link check covers Linux x64 only;
do not treat it as validation of Linux ARM64's minimum glibc version.

On an upstream upgrade, review these changes individually against that
tag's build scripts and tool packages. Drop mappings, discovery rules, and
the compiler-rt override when upstream handles the corresponding case.
Reconsider Windows ARM64's tool selection as part of the planned v145
upgrade instead of treating the old emulation mapping as the final design.

Upstream build and tool discovery:
https://github.com/denoland/rusty_v8/blob/v0.106.0/build.rs
https://github.com/denoland/rusty_v8/blob/v0.106.0/tools/ninja_gn_binaries.py
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+/c6d44e625aa64fa89cbdc971dfd301353bee04f3/vs_toolchain.py

